A.lyF=new B.r("Paris hosts the Olympic Games, women compete for the first time",1900,"The 1900 Games were stretched over five months as a side-show to the World's Fair. Twenty-two women competed \u2014 in tennis, golf, croquet and sailing.")
A.lB7=new B.r("Queen Victoria dies after 64 years on the throne",1901,"Her reign was so long that most Britons had known no other monarch. She was also the first royal photographed extensively \u2014 an early celebrity of the camera age.")
A.luo=new B.r(u.bh,1903,"The flight lasted 12 seconds and covered 37 metres \u2014 shorter than the wingspan of a modern jumbo jet. Only five people watched it happen.")
A.lCB=new B.r("Albert Einstein publishes the theory of special relativity",1905,"Einstein was 26 and working as a patent clerk in Bern. He wrote four world-changing papers that year \u2014 his so-called 'miracle year'.")
A.lBY=new B.r("Ford releases the Model T motor car",1908,"It cost $850 at launch and $260 fifteen years later \u2014 Ford kept slashing prices as the assembly line got faster. Half of all cars on Earth were Model Ts by 1918.")
A.lvD=new B.r("The Titanic sinks on her maiden voyage",1912,"Wireless radio was still a novelty in 1912 \u2014 the SOS distress code had only existed for a few years. Marconi operators on ships nearby became household names overnight.")
A.lBp=new B.r("World War I begins in Europe",1914,"Both sides expected the war to be over by Christmas. It shaped the map of the modern world and gave English words like 'trench', 'no-man's land' and 'over the top'.")
A.lCX=new B.r("World War I ends on the 11th hour of the 11th day of the 11th month",1918,"The armistice took effect at exactly 11:00 on 11 November. Church bells rang across Britain for the first time in years.")
A.lCu=new B.r(u.hA,1919,"The two aviators landed in a bog in Connemara after 16 hours in an open cockpit. Their prize: \xa310,000 from a British newspaper.")
A.lC0=new B.r("Women win the right to vote in the United States",1920,"The 19th Amendment was ratified after decades of campaigning. New Zealand had been first in 1893; the US was one of many countries to follow through the 1920s.")
A.lCg=new B.r("The first commercial radio broadcast goes on air",1920,"Station KDKA in Pittsburgh reported the US presidential election live. Within two years there were 500 stations across America.")
A.lyu=new B.r("The first Winter Olympics are held in Chamonix, France",1924,"Only 16 nations competed. Figure skating had been at the Summer Games before \u2014 organisers finally admitted it made more sense on actual ice.")
A.lzC=new B.r("The first television picture is transmitted",1927,"The first image was a dollar sign, sent by inventor Philo Farnsworth. Home TV sets took another 20 years to become common.")
A.lBx=new B.r("Charles Lindbergh flies solo across the Atlantic",1927,"He stayed awake for 33 hours. On landing in Paris, 150,000 people rushed the runway and carried him overhead.")
A.lud=new B.r("Alexander Fleming discovers penicillin",1928,"He spotted it on a mouldy petri dish he'd left out over the summer. It took another decade of work to turn the accident into a life-saving drug.")
A.lCy=new B.r("The Wall Street Crash triggers the Great Depression",1929,"The crash unfolded over several days. In its wake the term 'blue chip' became popular \u2014 meaning the sturdiest, most reliable companies left standing.")
A.lAR=new B.r("The first Academy Awards ceremony is held",1929,"The whole event lasted 15 minutes and was really a dinner. Winners had been announced in the newspaper three months earlier.")
A.lz_=new B.r("Uruguay hosts and wins the first FIFA World Cup",1930,"Only 13 nations turned up \u2014 the boat trip from Europe took two weeks. Uruguay won on home soil.")
A.lzW=new B.r("Amelia Earhart flies solo across the Atlantic",1932,"She landed in a cow pasture in Northern Ireland after 15 hours. She was the first woman \u2014 and second person ever \u2014 to fly the Atlantic alone.")
A.lwV=new B.r("The Monopoly board game is released commercially",1935,"The original design was meant to teach players about the dangers of landlords. Somewhere along the way the message got lost.")
A.lAJ=new B.r("Edward VIII abdicates the British throne",1936,"He gave up the crown to marry an American divorc\xe9e. His reign lasted less than a year \u2014 the shortest of any modern British monarch.")
A.lvv=new B.r("Snow White and the Seven Dwarfs premieres",1937,"Walt Disney mortgaged his house to finance the first full-length animated feature. Hollywood called it 'Disney's Folly' \u2014 until it became one of the highest-grossing films of the decade.")
A.lvM=new B.r("The Golden Gate Bridge opens in San Francisco",1937,"It was the longest suspension bridge in the world until 1964. The famous orange colour was chosen to stand out in the fog.")
A.lx0=new B.r("The Wizard of Oz is released in cinemas",1939,"Dorothy's ruby slippers were silver in the original book. They were changed to red so they'd pop on Technicolor film.")
A.lBr=new B.r("Casablanca premieres in cinemas",1942,"Nobody knew how the film would end during filming \u2014 the writers were still finalising the airport scene as the cameras rolled.")
A.lvz=new B.r("World War II ends",1945,"Street parties broke out across Britain, France and much of the world. VE Day in London reportedly ran out of beer by nightfall.")
A.lBF=new B.r("The first modern computer, ENIAC, is switched on",1946,"It weighed 27 tonnes and filled a whole room. Your phone is roughly a million times more powerful.")
A.lCA=new B.r("India gains independence from Britain",1947,"The transfer of power happened at midnight. Jawaharlal Nehru's 'tryst with destiny' speech is still taught in schools across India.")
A.lCv=new B.r("The State of Israel is founded",1948,"The declaration was read out in Tel Aviv on a Friday afternoon. The document itself was drafted in a rush over just a few days.")
A.lyo=new B.r("The LP vinyl record is introduced",1948,"Before the LP, an 'album' meant a book of 78-rpm shellac discs. Long-play vinyl fit a whole symphony on a single side.")
A.lCt=new B.r("The Peanuts comic strip debuts in newspapers",1950,"Charles Schulz drew nearly every strip himself for 50 years \u2014 around 17,000 in total. Snoopy first walked on two legs six years in.")
A.lxR=new B.r("Elizabeth II is crowned Queen",1953,"It was the first coronation broadcast on TV. Millions of British families bought their first television set just to watch it.")
A.lwD=new B.r("Watson and Crick describe the DNA double helix",1953,"Their famous paper in Nature was just one page long. It included a single sketch that changed biology forever.")
A.lCn=new B.r(u.ib,1954,"Bannister ran the record on his lunch break from medical school. Six weeks later an Australian broke it again \u2014 the barrier fell twice in one summer.")
A.lBa=new B.r("Elvis Presley records his first song at Sun Studio",1954,"The take was almost accidental \u2014 Elvis was clowning around between sessions when the engineer hit record. Rock and roll's origin story is basically a happy studio blooper.")
A.lAh=new B.r("Rosa Parks refuses to give up her bus seat",1955,"The Montgomery bus boycott that followed lasted 381 days. Parks kept working as a seamstress throughout.")
