A.lBf=new B.r("The Wright brothers make the first powered aeroplane flight",1903,"At Kitty Hawk the first hop lasted 12 seconds and covered about 37 metres \u2014 shorter than the wingspan of a modern jumbo jet.")
A.lvo=new B.r("Cunard's liner Mauretania enters service as the fastest ship afloat",1907,"She soon claimed the Blue Riband for the fastest Atlantic crossing and held the title for around two decades \u2014 a record run for any ocean liner.")
A.lwd=new B.r("Ford launches the Model T motor car",1908,"It started at 850 dollars and fell to around 260 as the assembly line sped up. By 1918 roughly half the cars on Earth were Model Ts.")
A.lCx=new B.r("Ford introduces the moving assembly line for car production",1913,"The time to build a Model T dropped from over 12 hours to about 90 minutes. The idea was borrowed partly from meat-packing plants.")
A.lvc=new B.r("The Panama Canal opens, linking the Atlantic and Pacific",1914,"Ships no longer had to sail all the way around South America. The route cut roughly 13,000 km off a voyage from New York to San Francisco.")
A.lyj=new B.r(u.hA,1919,"The two aviators landed in a bog in Connemara after about 16 hours in an open cockpit. Their prize was 10,000 pounds from a newspaper.")
A.lBe=new B.r("The Flying Scotsman locomotive enters service",1923,"It later became the first steam engine officially recorded at 100 mph. The locomotive is still preserved and runs on heritage lines today.")
A.lwj=new B.r("Route 66 is established across the United States",1926,"Running from Chicago to Santa Monica, it stretched around 3,940 km. It became one of the most famous roads in the world, celebrated in song and film.")
A.lxD=new B.r("The Southern Cross makes the first flight across the Pacific",1928,"Charles Kingsford Smith and his crew flew from California to Australia in stages. The longest leg kept them airborne for more than 30 hours.")
A.lAN=new B.r("Frank Whittle patents the turbojet engine",1930,"He was a young RAF officer at the time. His design would go on to power the jet age, though it took another decade to fly.")
A.lzG=new B.r("The Douglas DC-3 airliner makes its first flight",1935,"It was the first airliner that could make money carrying passengers alone. Many DC-3s built in the 1930s and 40s are still flying today.")
A.lu2=new B.r("The first Volkswagen Beetles are built",1938,"Its rounded shape and rear engine made it instantly recognisable. The Beetle went on to become one of the best-selling cars ever made.")
A.lze=new B.r("The locomotive Mallard sets the steam speed record at 126 mph",1938,"The run down Stoke Bank in England has never been beaten by another steam engine. Mallard is now preserved in the National Railway Museum.")
A.lui=new B.r("Chuck Yeager breaks the sound barrier in the Bell X-1",1947,"He became the first person to fly faster than sound in level flight. He named the rocket plane 'Glamorous Glennis' after his wife.")
A.lzx=new B.r("The Land Rover is launched",1948,"Its aluminium body was a clever workaround for post-war steel shortages. The rugged design stayed in production, barely changed, for decades.")
A.lwu=new B.r("The de Havilland Comet, the first jet airliner, takes flight",1949,"It flew higher, faster and more smoothly than propeller planes. The Comet ushered in the jet travel we still know today.")
A.luk=new B.r("The first container ship sets sail, launching modern shipping",1956,"The Ideal X carried 58 metal boxes on its first voyage. Standard containers went on to transform global trade and cut shipping costs hugely.")
A.lwA=new B.r("The Boeing 707 makes its first flight",1957,"It made jet travel mainstream in America and beyond. Crossing the Atlantic suddenly took hours rather than the better part of a day.")
A.lyG=new B.r("The Mini is launched",1959,"Its clever sideways engine freed up cabin space in a tiny footprint. The design became a British icon and a rally-winning giant-killer.")
A.lul=new B.r("The first hovercraft crosses the English Channel",1959,"The SR.N1 rode across on a cushion of air. Passenger hovercraft later ferried travellers between England and France for decades.")
A.lx3=new B.r("The Jaguar E-Type sports car debuts in Geneva",1961,"Its long bonnet and flowing curves drew instant praise. It has been called one of the most beautiful cars ever made.")
A.luQ=new B.r("Japan opens the Shinkansen, the first bullet train",1964,"Trains ran between Tokyo and Osaka at around 210 km/h \u2014 remarkable for the time. It set the template for high-speed rail worldwide.")
A.lCb=new B.r("Ford puts the Mustang on sale",1964,"It sold around a million cars in under two years. The Mustang created a whole new class of affordable, sporty 'pony cars'.")
A.lzE=new B.r("The Saturn V rocket makes its first launch",1967,"Standing 111 metres tall, it remains one of the most powerful rockets ever flown. It would soon carry astronauts toward the Moon.")
A.lAO=new B.r("The Boeing 747 'Jumbo Jet' makes its first flight",1969,"Its upper-deck hump became one of the most recognisable shapes in the sky. The 747 made long-haul travel affordable for millions.")
A.lAb=new B.r("The Boeing 747 enters passenger service",1970,"The first flight ran from New York to London. Carrying around 350 passengers, it roughly doubled the size of a typical airliner.")
A.lyR=new B.r("Volkswagen launches the Golf",1974,"It carried the torch as the Beetle wound down. The Golf became one of the best-selling cars in the world in its own right.")
A.lv7=new B.r("Concorde enters commercial supersonic service",1976,"It crossed the Atlantic in under three and a half hours at twice the speed of sound. Passengers dined on silver service the whole way.")
A.lA5=new B.r("France opens the TGV high-speed rail line",1981,"The first route linked Paris and Lyon at around 260 km/h. It made the train faster than flying for many journeys across France.")
A.lCZ=new B.r("The DeLorean DMC-12 goes into production",1981,"Its brushed stainless-steel body and gull-wing doors were unlike anything else. A few years later it found lasting fame on the big screen.")
A.lAo=new B.r("The Rutan Voyager flies non-stop around the world without refuelling",1986,"It circled the globe in just over nine days on a single tank. Most of the featherweight aircraft was built from lightweight composite materials.")
A.lya=new B.r(u.h,1994,"The tunnel is 50 km long, most of it under the sea. Teams digging from both sides met in the middle within 15 cm of each other.")
A.luB=new B.r("Eurostar begins passenger service through the Channel Tunnel",1994,"Trains linked London directly with Paris and Brussels. Travellers could now go city-centre to city-centre without ever boarding a plane.")
A.lw3=new B.r("ThrustSSC becomes the first car to break the sound barrier on land",1997,"The jet-powered car reached over 1,220 km/h in the Nevada desert. It set a world land speed record that still stands.")
A.lyc=new B.r("The Segway personal transporter is unveiled",2001,"The self-balancing two-wheeler stayed upright using gyroscopes and sensors. It became a familiar sight on city tours around the world.")
A.lyP=new B.r("Concorde makes its final commercial flight",2003,"The last flight touched down at Heathrow on 24 October to a champagne welcome. No supersonic airliner has flown scheduled service since.")
A.lzd=new B.r("The Tesla Roadster, an early long-range electric sports car, ships",2008,"It used thousands of laptop-style battery cells to reach highway speeds with real range. It showed electric cars could be genuinely quick and fun.")
A.lxm=new B.r("The Nissan Leaf launches and becomes a best-selling electric car",2010,"It was one of the first mass-market EVs built for everyday families. For years it was the best-selling electric car in the world.")
A.lD2=new B.r("Tesla begins delivering the Model S",2012,"The all-electric saloon won wide praise for its range and software. Its large touchscreen dashboard influenced car design across the industry.")
A.lwE=new B.r("SpaceX lands a Falcon 9 rocket booster upright for the first time",2015,"The booster flew back and touched down on its landing legs. Reusing rockets this way promised to make spaceflight far cheaper.")
A.lAY=new B.r("SpaceX Crew Dragon carries astronauts to orbit for the first time",2020,"It was the first crewed orbital launch from US soil in nearly a decade. The capsule docked smoothly with the International Space Station.")
