A.luZ=new B.r("Georges M\xe9li\xe8s releases A Trip to the Moon",1902,"This French silent short is often called the first science-fiction film. Its image of a rocket lodged in the Moon's eye is still one of cinema's most recognisable pictures.")
A.lyE=new B.r("The Great Train Robbery pioneers narrative film",1903,"Edwin S. Porter's 12-minute Western was one of the first films to tell a real story with editing. Its closing shot of an outlaw firing straight at the camera reportedly made audiences duck.")
A.lyn=new B.r("The Story of the Kelly Gang screens in Australia",1906,"Running over an hour, it is widely regarded as the world's first feature-length narrative film \u2014 beating Hollywood's features by several years.")
A.lA2=new B.r("Charlie Chaplin's Little Tramp makes his debut",1914,"Chaplin assembled the bowler hat, cane and oversized shoes almost by accident in a dressing room. The Tramp went on to become the most famous figure of the silent era.")
A.lwz=new B.r("United Artists is founded by the stars themselves",1919,"Chaplin, Mary Pickford, Douglas Fairbanks and director D.W. Griffith formed the studio so that artists \u2014 not executives \u2014 could control their own films.")
A.lxw=new B.r("Nosferatu brings the vampire to the screen",1922,"This unauthorised take on Dracula so angered Bram Stoker's widow that a court ordered every print destroyed. A few copies survived, which is the only reason we can watch it today.")
A.lC2=new B.r("The Jazz Singer ends the silent era",1927,"It was the first feature with synchronised spoken dialogue. Al Jolson's line \"You ain't heard nothin' yet\" turned out to be literally true for the whole industry.")
A.lBC=new B.r("Steamboat Willie introduces Mickey Mouse",1928,"One of the first cartoons with synchronised sound, it launched Mickey Mouse. Walt Disney himself provided the character's original squeaky voice.")
A.lxL=new B.r("Disney releases Snow White and the Seven Dwarfs",1937,'Hollywood mocked it as "Disney\'s Folly" \u2014 nobody believed people would sit through a feature-length cartoon. It became the highest-grossing film of its day.')
A.lAr=new B.r("The Wizard of Oz dazzles with Technicolor",1939,"The film opens in sepia and bursts into colour the moment Dorothy steps into Oz. Judy Garland's ruby slippers are now among the most prized objects in film history.")
A.lCQ=new B.r("Gone with the Wind sweeps the box office",1939,"Adjusted for inflation it remains the highest-grossing film ever made. Hattie McDaniel's win also made her the first Black performer to receive an Academy Award.")
A.lyS=new B.r("Orson Welles releases Citizen Kane",1941,'Welles was only 25 when he directed, co-wrote and starred in it. Regularly voted one of the greatest films ever made, it turns on a single whispered word: "Rosebud."')
A.luJ=new B.r("Casablanca premieres in wartime",1942,"The script was still being rewritten during filming, so the cast didn't know how it would end. It won Best Picture and gave us \"Here's looking at you, kid.\"")
A.luG=new B.r("Bicycle Thieves defines Italian neorealism",1948,"Vittorio De Sica shot on the real streets of Rome using non-professional actors. Its raw, everyday realism reshaped how films around the world were made.")
A.lxG=new B.r("Kurosawa's Rashomon wins at Venice",1950,'Its story of one event told through conflicting eyewitness accounts gave us the phrase "the Rashomon effect." The Golden Lion win opened Japanese cinema to the West.')
A.lw9=new B.r("The first coast-to-coast colour TV broadcast airs",1954,"NBC transmitted the Tournament of Roses Parade in colour on New Year's Day. Almost nobody owned a colour set yet, so most viewers still watched it in black and white.")
A.lCH=new B.r("Seven Samurai sets the ensemble-team template",1954,"Kurosawa's tale of villagers hiring warriors created the blueprint for countless team-assembles-for-a-mission films, and was remade in Hollywood as The Magnificent Seven.")
A.luD=new B.r("The 400 Blows launches the French New Wave",1959,"Fran\xe7ois Truffaut's semi-autobiographical debut helped kick off the French New Wave. Its final freeze-frame on the young hero's face is one of cinema's most quoted endings.")
A.lxb=new B.r("Hitchcock's Psycho shocks audiences",1960,"Hitchcock insisted no one be admitted once the film had begun. The shower scene runs about 45 seconds and used dozens of quick cuts to imply far more than it showed.")
A.lBq=new B.r("2001: A Space Odyssey redefines effects",1968,"Stanley Kubrick's visual effects were so far ahead of their time they still hold up today. Its calm, murderous computer HAL 9000 became a lasting symbol of AI gone wrong.")
A.lws=new B.r("The world watches the Moon landing live on TV",1969,"An estimated 600 million people tuned in to see Apollo 11 \u2014 the largest television audience the planet had ever gathered for a single live event.")
A.lBs=new B.r("The Godfather arrives",1972,"Based on Mario Puzo's novel, it revived Marlon Brando's career. He won Best Actor but boycotted the ceremony in protest at Hollywood's portrayal of Native Americans.")
A.lwF=new B.r("Sholay becomes a Bollywood legend",1975,'This "curry western" ran continuously in some Indian cinemas for over five years. Its characters and dialogue are still quoted across India half a century later.')
A.lwv=new B.r("Star Wars: A New Hope opens in cinemas",1977,"Fox gave George Lucas the merchandising rights instead of a bigger fee \u2014 a decision that made him a billionaire.")
A.lD5=new B.r("MTV launches and reshapes pop culture",1981,'The very first video it aired was, fittingly, "Video Killed the Radio Star" by The Buggles. Music television went on to define a generation of pop.')
A.lCW=new B.r("E.T. the Extra-Terrestrial charms the world",1982,"Spielberg's film became the highest-grossing movie of its time. A trail of Reese's Pieces led the alien home after M&M's famously turned the placement down.")
A.lvU=new B.r("Studio Ghibli releases My Neighbor Totoro",1988,"Hayao Miyazaki's gentle forest spirit was such a hit that Totoro became the studio's official mascot, appearing in the Ghibli logo ever since.")
A.lxi=new B.r("The Simpsons premieres as a half-hour series",1989,"Debuting just before Christmas, it grew into the longest-running scripted primetime series in American television history.")
A.luY=new B.r("Jurassic Park brings dinosaurs to life",1993,"Spielberg blended animatronics with early computer graphics so seamlessly that audiences believed the dinosaurs were real. It marked a turning point for visual effects.")
A.lyM=new B.r("Pixar releases Toy Story",1995,"It was the first feature film animated entirely on computers. The gamble launched Pixar as a powerhouse and changed animation permanently.")
A.lAa=new B.r("Titanic sails to record box office",1997,"James Cameron's epic was the first film to gross a billion dollars worldwide. It tied the all-time record with 11 Academy Awards.")
A.lwh=new B.r("Spirited Away wins the animation Oscar",2001,"Miyazaki's fantasy out-grossed Titanic in Japan and became the first hand-drawn, non-English film to win the Academy Award for Best Animated Feature.")
A.lCP=new B.r("The Lord of the Rings: The Return of the King sweeps the Oscars",2003,"It won all 11 awards it was nominated for, tying the record set by Ben-Hur and Titanic. No film has ever gone a cleaner night at the Academy Awards.")
A.lw2=new B.r("Netflix launches streaming",2007,'Still mainly a DVD-by-mail company, Netflix added a "watch instantly" feature that let subscribers stream online. It quietly began the era that reshaped how the world watches.')
A.lvR=new B.r("Avatar ushers in the 3D boom",2009,"James Cameron's blue-hued world became the highest-grossing film ever and sent cinemas racing to install 3D screens around the globe.")
A.lyt=new B.r("The Avengers proves the shared-universe model",2012,"By finally teaming up heroes from separate films, Marvel showed that an interconnected movie universe could work \u2014 a formula studios have chased ever since.")
A.lBV=new B.r("The Oscars announce the wrong Best Picture",2017,"La La Land was declared the winner and its team was mid-speech when it emerged the real Best Picture was Moonlight. A mixed-up envelope caused the most dramatic gaffe in Oscar history.")
A.lCo=new B.r("Parasite wins the Palme d'Or at Cannes",2019,"Bong Joon-ho's dark satire was the first Korean film to take Cannes' top prize. Months later it would make history again at the Oscars.")
A.lyX=new B.r("Squid Game becomes a global phenomenon",2021,"The Korean survival drama became Netflix's most-watched series launch to that point, topping charts in more than 90 countries within weeks.")
A.lB9=new B.r("Barbenheimer takes over cinemas",2023,"Barbie and Oppenheimer opened on the very same day, and audiences turned the odd pairing into a double-feature event that revived the post-pandemic box office.")
A.lyr=new B.r("Everything Everywhere All at Once sweeps the Oscars",2023,"The genre-bending indie won seven Academy Awards including Best Picture, and Michelle Yeoh became the first Asian performer to win Best Actress.")
