A.lzT=new B.r(u.bh,1903,"The whole first flight at Kitty Hawk lasted 12 seconds and covered 120 feet \u2014 shorter than the wingspan of a modern airliner.")
A.lAH=new B.r("Ford launches the Model T",1908,"Ford's moving assembly line later cut build time from over 12 hours to about 90 minutes, making the car affordable for ordinary families.")
A.lxE=new B.r("Regular public radio broadcasting begins in the US",1920,"Pittsburgh station KDKA aired live election results in November 1920, one of the first scheduled broadcasts to a paying home audience.")
A.lyQ=new B.r("John Logie Baird demonstrates the first working television",1926,"The Scottish inventor showed moving silhouette images to scientists in a London attic. Early sets scanned just 30 lines of picture.")
A.ly2=new B.r("The first transatlantic telephone service opens",1927,"A three-minute call between New York and London cost about $75 \u2014 a small fortune at the time \u2014 and travelled by radio, not cable.")
A.lva=new B.r("The ENIAC electronic computer is unveiled",1946,"Built in Pennsylvania, ENIAC filled a room, weighed 30 tons and used around 18,000 vacuum tubes to do its calculations.")
A.lAq=new B.r("Bell Labs invents the transistor",1947,"The tiny device that replaced bulky vacuum tubes made modern electronics possible and later earned its inventors a Nobel Prize.")
A.lAt=new B.r("Sony releases its first pocket transistor radio",1957,"The TR-63 helped launch Sony as a global brand. It was marketed as pocket-sized, though it was said to be a snug fit for most shirt pockets.")
A.lzD=new B.r("The Soviet Union launches Sputnik, the first satellite",1957,"The beach-ball-sized craft circled Earth every 96 minutes and its steady beeping could be picked up by amateur radios around the world.")
A.lAU=new B.r("The integrated circuit (microchip) is invented",1958,"Jack Kilby's first working chip at Texas Instruments packed a whole circuit onto one sliver of material \u2014 the seed of every modern gadget.")
A.lD7=new B.r("The first message is sent over ARPANET",1969,"Engineers tried to type 'LOGIN' between two California universities. The system crashed after 'LO' \u2014 a humble start for the internet.")
A.lvG=new B.r("Intel releases the 4004, the first commercial microprocessor",1971,"The entire computer 'brain' now fit on a single chip smaller than a fingernail, roughly matching the power of the room-sized ENIAC.")
A.lvr=new B.r("The first email is sent using the @ symbol",1971,"Ray Tomlinson chose @ to separate the user from the machine. He later admitted he couldn't recall what that very first test message said.")
A.lyB=new B.r(u.g_,1973,"Motorola's Martin Cooper called a rival from a New York street. The prototype weighed about a kilo and offered roughly 30 minutes of talk time.")
A.lxM=new B.r("Sony launches the Walkman personal cassette player",1979,"The Walkman made private, portable music normal for the first time. Early models even had two headphone jacks so friends could listen together.")
A.lzN=new B.r("IBM launches its first personal computer",1981,"The IBM PC made desktop computing respectable for business and set the standard that most later 'PC-compatible' machines followed.")
A.lvP=new B.r("The first commercial CD players go on sale",1982,"Developed jointly by Sony and Philips, the compact disc offered crisp digital sound and quickly began to push vinyl and cassettes aside.")
A.lup=new B.r("Apple airs its '1984' ad and launches the Macintosh",1984,"The Mac brought a mouse and on-screen icons to the mainstream. Its famous Super Bowl advert aired nationally only once.")
A.lyw=new B.r("Nintendo's Game Boy brings handheld gaming to the masses",1989,"Bundled with Tetris, the Game Boy's modest screen and long battery life beat flashier rivals and sold in the hundreds of millions.")
A.lzX=new B.r("Tim Berners-Lee proposes the World Wide Web at CERN",1989,"The British scientist's plan for linked documents was famously labelled 'vague but exciting' by his boss. The first website went live in 1991.")
A.lx6=new B.r("The first item is sold on the web via NetMarket",1994,"One of the first secure online purchases was reportedly a Sting CD \u2014 an early sign that people would happily shop over the internet.")
A.lBj=new B.r("Amazon sells its first book online",1995,"Jeff Bezos started in a garage selling books. Staff rang a bell for every order \u2014 a habit they dropped once the bell never stopped ringing.")
A.lvC=new B.r("DVD players reach the consumer market",1996,"First launched in Japan, the DVD held far more than a CD and gave film fans sharper picture and sound than the VHS tapes it replaced.")
A.lxK=new B.r("Google is founded",1998,"Larry Page and Sergey Brin ran their search engine from a rented garage. The name is a play on 'googol', the number one followed by 100 zeros.")
A.lwg=new B.r("Nokia's 3310 becomes a best-selling mobile phone",2000,"Famous for its near-indestructible build and the game Snake, the 3310 went on to sell well over 100 million units worldwide.")
A.lvw=new B.r("Wikipedia launches as a free online encyclopedia",2001,"Anyone could edit it, which sounded chaotic \u2014 yet within years it grew into one of the most visited reference sites on the planet.")
A.lwt=new B.r("Apple introduces the iPod",2001,"Marketed as '1,000 songs in your pocket', the iPod's click wheel and white earbuds turned it into a cultural icon almost overnight.")
A.lzi=new B.r("Skype launches free internet calling",2003,"Built by engineers in Estonia, Skype let people talk across the world for free and helped make video calls a normal part of everyday life.")
A.luU=new B.r("Facebook launches from a Harvard dorm room",2004,"It started as a student directory for one campus. Users first needed a university email address to join before it opened to the public.")
A.lum=new B.r("YouTube is founded and hosts its first video",2005,"The debut clip, 'Me at the zoo', ran just 19 seconds. Within a couple of years the site was serving billions of views a day.")
A.lxQ=new B.r("Apple unveils the first iPhone",2007,"Steve Jobs teased it as 'three revolutionary devices in one'. Nokia and BlackBerry didn't take the threat seriously for over a year.")
A.lvH=new B.r("Spotify launches music streaming in Europe",2008,"The Swedish service let people stream millions of songs on demand and offered a route away from piracy toward legal, instant listening.")
A.lCj=new B.r("Bitcoin's first block is mined",2009,"The mysterious creator known as Satoshi Nakamoto embedded a newspaper headline in the very first block, hinting at distrust of the banking system.")
A.lCL=new B.r("Apple launches the iPad",2010,"Critics mocked the name and doubted anyone needed a device between a phone and a laptop, yet tablets quickly sold by the millions.")
A.ly5=new B.r("Instagram launches as a photo-sharing app",2010,"It hit a million users in a couple of months. Its square photos were a nod to old Polaroid and Kodak Instamatic prints.")
A.lzm=new B.r("The Raspberry Pi credit-card-sized computer goes on sale",2012,"Designed by a UK charity to teach coding, the tiny, cheap board sold out on launch day and became a favourite of hobbyists everywhere.")
A.lCS=new B.r("TikTok launches internationally",2017,"Grown from China's Douyin, the short-video app's recommendation feed proved so addictive it became one of the fastest-growing platforms ever.")
A.lvA=new B.r("Nintendo releases the Switch hybrid console",2017,"The Switch worked both as a home console and a handheld. That flexibility helped it become one of the best-selling consoles of all time.")
A.lAK=new B.r("OpenAI releases ChatGPT to the public",2022,"The chatbot reached an estimated 100 million users in about two months, making it one of the fastest-adopted apps in history.")
A.lzM=new B.r("Apple releases the Vision Pro headset",2024,"Billed as 'spatial computing', the headset let wearers place apps around the room and drew as much attention for its price as its technology.")
