A.lvX=new B.r("Enrico Caruso records ten arias in a Milan hotel room",1902,"The sessions proved opera stars could sell records, helping make Caruso one of the first truly global recording celebrities.")
A.lx5=new B.r("Reginald Fessenden broadcasts music by radio on Christmas Eve",1906,"He played 'O Holy Night' on violin over the airwaves. Ship operators expecting Morse code were startled to hear live music.")
A.lAv=new B.r("Irving Berlin publishes 'Alexander's Ragtime Band'",1911,"The song became a national craze and helped carry ragtime rhythms from sheet music into mainstream American pop.")
A.lwm=new B.r("The Original Dixieland Jass Band cuts the first jazz record",1917,"'Livery Stable Blues' sold in the hundreds of thousands and introduced the word 'jazz' to record buyers across the country.")
A.lv5=new B.r("Mamie Smith records 'Crazy Blues', an early blues vocal hit",1920,"Its runaway sales showed labels there was a huge audience for Black music and helped open the door to the blues recording boom.")
A.lz1=new B.r("The Bristol Sessions capture Jimmie Rodgers and the Carter Family",1927,"Often called the 'Big Bang of country music', the Tennessee recordings launched two founding acts of the genre in one week.")
A.lyI=new B.r("Louis Armstrong records 'West End Blues' with his Hot Five",1928,"Its soaring opening trumpet solo is still taught as the moment jazz shifted toward the soloist as an art form.")
A.lB4=new B.r("Benny Goodman ignites the Swing Era at the Palomar Ballroom",1935,"Dancers in Los Angeles erupted when the band cut loose with hot arrangements. The night is often marked as the big-band craze's start.")
A.luV=new B.r("Robert Johnson records his blues songs in a San Antonio hotel",1936,"He cut only 29 songs in his lifetime, yet they went on to shape rock and blues guitar for generations of players.")
A.lxt=new B.r("Benny Goodman brings swing to Carnegie Hall",1938,"Many doubted a jazz band belonged there. The sold-out concert proved swing could fill America's most prestigious concert hall.")
A.lAg=new B.r("Bing Crosby records 'White Christmas'",1942,"It went on to become the best-selling single of all time, a record it has held for decades.")
A.lBR=new B.r("Rodgers and Hammerstein's 'Oklahoma!' opens on Broadway",1943,"By weaving songs into the story rather than pausing for them, it reshaped how American musicals were written.")
A.lC6=new B.r("Columbia introduces the 33\u2153 rpm long-playing record",1948,"The LP could hold over 20 minutes a side, letting artists think in terms of full 'albums' for the first time.")
A.lua=new B.r("Elvis Presley records 'That's All Right' at Sun Studio, Memphis",1954,"The song blended country and blues into something new, and a local radio spin that same week set off immediate demand.")
A.lzb=new B.r("Chuck Berry releases 'Maybellene'",1955,"Its guitar-driven storytelling became a template for rock and roll songwriting that countless bands would follow.")
A.lx8=new B.r("Berry Gordy founds Motown Records in Detroit",1959,"Working from a small house he called 'Hitsville U.S.A.', Gordy built one of the most successful independent labels in music history.")
A.lCG=new B.r("Miles Davis releases 'Kind of Blue'",1959,"Recorded largely in first takes, it became the best-selling jazz album ever and a landmark of the modal jazz style.")
A.lyq=new B.r("The Beatles perform on 'The Ed Sullivan Show'",1964,"An estimated 73 million Americans tuned in \u2014 one of the era's largest TV audiences and the spark of the 'British Invasion'.")
A.luv=new B.r("Bob Dylan plays electric at the Newport Folk Festival",1965,"Swapping his acoustic guitar for an electric one divided the folk crowd and signaled a turning point toward folk-rock.")
A.lxT=new B.r("The Beach Boys release 'Pet Sounds'",1966,"Its lush studio layering pushed pop toward the album as an art form and influenced countless records that followed.")
A.lwX=new B.r("The Monterey Pop Festival draws tens of thousands to California",1967,"One of the first major rock festivals, it gave breakout US stages to artists like Jimi Hendrix and Otis Redding.")
A.lym=new B.r("Marvin Gaye releases 'What's Going On'",1971,"A flowing concept album on social themes, it broke from Motown's hit-single formula and is now considered a soul classic.")
A.luC=new B.r("Pink Floyd release 'The Dark Side of the Moon'",1973,"It went on to spend more than 900 weeks on the US album charts \u2014 one of the longest runs ever recorded.")
A.lvl=new B.r("DJ Kool Herc throws a Bronx block party seen as hip-hop's birth",1973,"By looping the danceable 'breaks' of records on two turntables, he laid the groundwork for an entire global genre.")
A.lAL=new B.r("Queen release 'Bohemian Rhapsody'",1975,"Nearly six minutes long with an operatic middle, it defied radio norms and became one of the best-loved singles ever.")
A.lu6=new B.r("Michael Jackson releases 'Thriller'",1982,"It became the best-selling album in history, and its cinematic music videos helped turn the format into an art of its own.")
