A.lC1=new B.r("The first solid eating chocolate bar goes on sale",1847,"British chocolatier J.S. Fry & Sons of Bristol mixed cocoa butter back into cocoa and sugar to mould a bar you could eat, instead of the drinking chocolate everyone knew before.")
A.lAB=new B.r("Levi's riveted blue jeans are patented",1873,"Tailor Jacob Davis and dry-goods merchant Levi Strauss patented copper rivets at the stress points of work trousers. The rivets stopped pockets from tearing and created the modern jean.")
A.lCU=new B.r("Coca-Cola is first sold",1886,"Atlanta pharmacist John Pemberton mixed the first syrup and sold it at a soda fountain for five cents a glass. It was marketed at first as a tonic rather than a soft drink.")
A.lz0=new B.r("The Swiss Army knife is born",1891,"Karl Elsener began supplying the Swiss army with a folding knife that combined a blade, screwdriver, can opener and reamer. His company later took the name Victorinox.")
A.lv0=new B.r("Toothpaste arrives in a squeezable tube",1896,"Colgate began selling toothpaste in the collapsible metal tube we still recognise today. Before that, most people scooped tooth powder or paste from a shared jar.")
A.lzZ=new B.r("The teddy bear appears in toy shops",1902,"Named after US President Theodore 'Teddy' Roosevelt, the stuffed bear was launched almost simultaneously by Morris Michtom in New York and the Steiff company in Germany.")
A.ly8=new B.r("Crayola crayons go on sale",1903,"Binney & Smith sold the first box of eight Crayola crayons for a nickel. The name blends the French 'craie' (chalk) with 'oleaginous', meaning oily.")
A.lxN=new B.r("Kellogg's Corn Flakes launch",1906,"Will Keith Kellogg turned a flaked-grain recipe he stumbled on with his brother into a packaged breakfast cereal, founding the company that bore his name in Battle Creek, Michigan.")
A.luz=new B.r("The modern zipper is perfected",1913,"Swedish-American engineer Gideon Sundback designed the interlocking tooth-and-slider fastener that actually stayed shut. The catchy name 'zipper' came a decade later from a rubber-boot maker.")
A.luw=new B.r("Keds bring the first mass-market sneaker",1917,"Keds paired a canvas upper with a rubber sole to make a shoe quiet enough to sneak around in \u2014 hence 'sneaker'. The same year Converse released its All Star basketball shoe.")
A.lxf=new B.r("Kleenex tissues are introduced",1924,"Kimberly-Clark first marketed Kleenex as a way to remove cold cream. Customers kept using them to blow their noses, so the company leaned into the disposable handkerchief instead.")
A.luP=new B.r("Sliced bread is sold for the first time",1928,"Otto Rohwedder's bread-slicing machine debuted at a bakery in Chillicothe, Missouri. It was such a hit that 'the greatest thing since sliced bread' became a byword for innovation.")
A.lBH=new B.r("Scotch transparent tape hits the market",1930,"3M engineer Richard Drew invented a clear cellophane adhesive tape during the Depression, when people wanted to mend things rather than replace them.")
A.lAs=new B.r("Nescaf\xe9 makes instant coffee a staple",1938,"Swiss company Nestl\xe9 launched a soluble coffee powder that kept for months and dissolved in hot water, developed partly to use up a Brazilian coffee surplus.")
A.lAz=new B.r("The chocolate chip cookie is invented",1938,"Ruth Wakefield of the Toll House Inn in Massachusetts chopped a bar of chocolate into her cookie dough. The chunks held their shape, and a classic was born.")
A.lB2=new B.r("Duct tape is invented",1942,"Developed during World War II to seal ammunition cases against water, the strong cloth-backed tape was originally green and nicknamed 'duck tape' for how it shrugged off moisture.")
A.lur=new B.r("The ballpoint pen goes on sale",1945,"Based on L\xe1szl\xf3 B\xedr\xf3's design, the Reynolds Rocket sold out on its first day at a New York department store. A ball bearing rolled ink smoothly without the blots of a fountain pen.")
A.lCs=new B.r("Tupperware seals in the kitchen",1946,"Earl Tupper designed airtight plastic containers with a 'burping' lid. Sales only took off once Brownie Wise pioneered the home Tupperware party to demonstrate the seal.")
A.lxq=new B.r("The microwave oven is first sold",1947,"Raytheon's Radarange grew out of engineer Percy Spencer noticing a chocolate bar melt near a radar magnetron. The first units were nearly two metres tall and sold to restaurants.")
A.lxl=new B.r("The first credit card is issued",1950,"Diners Club launched a cardboard charge card accepted at a handful of New York restaurants. The idea reportedly came after founder Frank McNamara forgot his wallet at dinner.")
A.lwN=new B.r("Velcro is patented",1955,"Swiss engineer George de Mestral got the idea after burrs stuck to his dog's fur on a walk. He paired tiny hooks with soft loops and named it from the French 'velours' and 'crochet'.")
A.ly_=new B.r("The modern LEGO brick clicks into place",1958,"Denmark's LEGO added the stud-and-tube coupling that lets bricks grip tightly yet pull apart. A brick made today still snaps onto one moulded that year.")
A.lyh=new B.r("Instant ramen is invented",1958,"Momofuku Ando of Japan's Nissin launched Chikin Ramen, flash-frying noodles so they cooked in minutes with hot water. It reshaped the way the world eats a quick meal.")
A.lB6=new B.r("The Barbie doll debuts",1959,"Mattel's Ruth Handler introduced Barbie at the New York Toy Fair after noticing her daughter preferred adult-looking paper dolls. The doll was named after that daughter, Barbara.")
A.lug=new B.r("The Etch A Sketch goes on sale",1960,"Invented in France by Andr\xe9 Cassagnes and licensed by Ohio Art, the red drawing toy uses two knobs to steer a stylus through aluminium powder behind the glass.")
A.lBZ=new B.r("Pampers make disposable diapers mainstream",1961,"A Procter & Gamble engineer, tired of washing cloth nappies for his grandchild, helped create a throwaway diaper. Pampers rolled out to test markets and quickly caught on.")
A.lzQ=new B.r("Nutella spreads across the breakfast table",1964,"Italy's Ferrero reworked a wartime hazelnut-cocoa paste, created when chocolate was scarce, into a smooth spreadable jar and gave it the name Nutella.")
A.lCl=new B.r("The Ziploc resealable bag arrives",1968,"The press-together plastic zipper seal, adapted from an earlier Danish invention, gave households a bag they could open and close again to keep food fresh.")
A.lvF=new B.r("Cup Noodles reinvents fast food",1971,"Nissin's Momofuku Ando packed instant noodles into a waterproof foam cup so they could be eaten anywhere with just hot water \u2014 no bowl or cooking required.")
A.lAp=new B.r("The disposable Bic lighter is launched",1973,"France's Bic applied the same throwaway logic it used for pens to the cigarette lighter, selling a cheap plastic flame good for thousands of lights before being tossed.")
A.lus=new B.r("The first barcode is scanned at a checkout",1974,"A pack of Wrigley's chewing gum became the first product rung up by its Universal Product Code, at a supermarket in Troy, Ohio, launching the age of the checkout beep.")
A.lBg=new B.r("Sony releases the Walkman",1979,"Japan's Sony put a cassette player in your pocket with headphones, letting people carry a personal soundtrack anywhere for the first time and changing how the world listened to music.")
A.lBh=new B.r("The Rubik's Cube goes on sale worldwide",1980,"Hungarian professor Ern\u0151 Rubik invented it in 1974 to teach 3D geometry. It took him a month to solve his own creation before it became the best-selling puzzle in history.")
A.lAF=new B.r("3M launches the Post-it Note",1980,"A weak adhesive that scientist Spencer Silver couldn't find a use for met colleague Art Fry's need to bookmark his hymnal. Together they made the sticky note that pulls off cleanly.")
A.lB8=new B.r("Nespresso brews its first capsule coffee",1986,"Switzerland's Nestl\xe9 launched a system that pierced a sealed pod of ground coffee to make a single espresso, aiming to bring caf\xe9-style coffee into the home and office.")
A.lvk=new B.r("The first supermarket self-checkout is installed",1986,"David Humble's CheckRobot system let shoppers scan and bag their own groceries, debuting at a Kroger-owned store in Georgia \u2014 the ancestor of today's self-service lanes.")
A.lyd=new B.r("Nintendo releases the Game Boy",1989,"Japan's Nintendo sold a handheld console with swappable cartridges and a monochrome screen. Bundled with Tetris, it put video games in pockets around the world.")
A.lCp=new B.r("The Super Soaker water gun launches",1990,"NASA engineer Lonnie Johnson invented a pressure-pumped water gun while tinkering with a heat-pump idea at home. It became one of the best-selling toys of the decade.")
A.lAI=new B.r("The USB flash drive reaches consumers",2000,"Small enough for a keychain and needing no batteries or cables, the plug-in memory stick replaced the floppy disk and let people carry files in their pocket.")
A.luO=new B.r("Apple unveils the iPhone",2007,"Steve Jobs introduced a phone, a music player and an internet device in one glass touchscreen. It merged the everyday gadgets people carried into a single pocket computer.")
