A.lvg=new B.r("Magnavox releases the Odyssey, the first home console",1972,"Designed by Ralph Baer, it plugged into a TV and shipped with plastic overlays instead of on-screen graphics. It proved people would play games at home, not just in arcades.")
A.lyT=new B.r("Atari launches Pong in arcades",1972,"The simple two-paddle tennis game became the first commercially successful video game and kicked off the arcade industry.")
A.lxj=new B.r("Atari releases the 2600 (Video Computer System)",1977,"Its interchangeable cartridges let one machine play many games, a model that would define home consoles for decades.")
A.lzL=new B.r("Taito releases Space Invaders",1978,"The alien-shooting hit was so popular in Japan that it was rumored to cause a coin shortage, and it made the high-score chase a staple.")
A.lwn=new B.r("Atari releases Asteroids",1979,"Its crisp vector graphics and addictive gameplay made it one of Atari's biggest arcade successes and an early high-score classic.")
A.lAj=new B.r("Namco releases Pac-Man",1980,"The maze-chase game broke beyond the mostly male arcade audience and became a global pop-culture icon, spawning merchandise and a hit song.")
A.lwY=new B.r("Nintendo releases Donkey Kong",1981,"It introduced a jumping carpenter first called Jumpman, later renamed Mario, and launched Nintendo as an arcade powerhouse.")
A.lwS=new B.r("Alexey Pajitnov creates Tetris",1984,"Built by a Soviet programmer on an Elektronika 60, the falling-block puzzle became one of the best-selling games ever, especially after bundling with the Game Boy.")
A.lw6=new B.r("Nintendo releases Super Mario Bros",1985,"It launched with the NES in the US and rescued a video-game industry still reeling from the 1983 crash. Over 40 million copies eventually sold.")
A.lAu=new B.r("Nintendo launches the Game Boy",1989,"The handheld's long battery life and Tetris bundle made it a runaway hit, selling well over 100 million units worldwide.")
A.lwU=new B.r("Sega releases Sonic the Hedgehog",1991,"The speedy blue mascot gave the Genesis a rival to Mario and fueled Sega's aggressive marketing push against Nintendo.")
A.ly6=new B.r("id Software releases Doom",1993,"The fast, violent first-person shooter popularized the genre, online deathmatch, and modding, and spread widely as shareware.")
A.lyb=new B.r("Sony launches the PlayStation",1994,"Debuting in Japan, Sony's CD-based console brought 3D gaming to the mainstream and quickly became the market leader.")
A.lB1=new B.r("Nintendo releases Super Mario 64",1996,"A launch title for the Nintendo 64, it set the template for 3D platformers with free-roaming camera and analog-stick movement.")
A.lCh=new B.r("Blizzard releases StarCraft",1998,"The real-time strategy game became a national pastime in South Korea, helping give birth to professional esports leagues and televised matches.")
A.lye=new B.r("Sony launches the PlayStation 2",2000,"Doubling as a DVD player, it became the best-selling console of all time with more than 155 million units sold.")
A.lvI=new B.r("Microsoft launches the Xbox with Halo: Combat Evolved",2001,"Halo turned console first-person shooters mainstream and made the Xbox a serious contender in Sony and Nintendo's market.")
A.lxY=new B.r("Blizzard releases World of Warcraft",2004,"The massively multiplayer online game grew to over 10 million subscribers and defined the MMORPG genre for a generation.")
A.lAE=new B.r("Nintendo launches the Wii",2006,"Its motion controls drew in families and non-gamers, letting Nintendo outsell more powerful rivals during that console cycle.")
A.ly7=new B.r("Rovio releases Angry Birds",2009,"The physics-based mobile hit showed that smartphones were a major gaming platform, racking up hundreds of millions of downloads.")
A.lAP=new B.r("Mojang releases Minecraft's full version",2011,"The blocky sandbox built by Markus Persson became one of the best-selling games ever and a cultural staple for young players.")
A.lA1=new B.r("Rockstar releases Grand Theft Auto V",2013,"It earned about a billion dollars in its first three days and grew into one of the most profitable entertainment products of all time.")
A.lBE=new B.r("Niantic releases Pok\xe9mon GO",2016,"The augmented-reality mobile game sent crowds outdoors to catch Pok\xe9mon and became a worldwide phenomenon within weeks.")
A.lCY=new B.r("Nintendo launches the Switch",2017,"The hybrid console worked both docked to a TV and as a handheld, reviving Nintendo's fortunes and selling over 100 million units.")
A.lBT=new B.r("Epic Games releases Fortnite Battle Royale",2017,"Its free-to-play last-player-standing mode exploded into a global sensation, reshaping how games make money and reach young audiences.")
A.lBP=new B.r("Sony launches the PlayStation 5",2020,"Released amid the pandemic, its next-gen graphics and fast SSD drove demand that outpaced supply for well over a year.")
A.lAn=new B.r("Microsoft launches the Xbox Series X",2020,"The most powerful Xbox to date leaned on Game Pass subscriptions, shifting Microsoft's focus toward services over hardware sales.")
A.lC8=new B.r("FromSoftware releases Elden Ring",2022,"The open-world action game, co-written with novelist George R. R. Martin, won Game of the Year and sold over 25 million copies.")
A.lxW=new B.r("Larian Studios releases Baldur's Gate 3",2023,"The sprawling role-playing game swept the year's top awards and showed that deep, story-rich single-player games could be huge hits.")
A.lBl=new B.r("Nintendo launches the Switch 2",2025,"The long-awaited successor to the original Switch arrived with more power and a larger screen while keeping the hybrid handheld design.")
